    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The smallest country of mainland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-america">Central America</a>, independent under its 1841 constitution after the federation collapsed.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">Coffee</a> built a powerful landowning elite; in 1932 the army’s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-matanza">Matanza</a> crushed a peasant and indigenous revolt in the west.</li><li>Civil war in 1980–1992 killed about 75,000; peace, dollarisation and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nayib-bukele">Nayib Bukele</a>’s anti-gang crackdown followed.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>El <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a> is the only Central American country with no <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> coastline: its whole shore, about 300 kilometres long, faces the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-ocean">Pacific Ocean</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

